      "writtenOn": "2026-06-21T09:55:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, I agree that this idempotent approach is overcomplicated.\n\nIt keeps the old API working, but the cost is too high: `existing_rule()` checks, label normalization, and validation of attrs from earlier macro calls. That is a lot of Starlark machinery for this problem.\n\nYour change helped clarify the better direction: make the `\u003cplugin\u003e__plugin_test_deps` target explicit instead of generating it from every `gerrit_plugin_tests()` call.\n\nI think we should still keep two concerns separate though:\n\n1. Gerrit\u0027s Eclipse classpath machinery expects the special `\u003cplugin\u003e__plugin_test_deps` target for plugins listed in `CUSTOM_PLUGINS_TEST_DEPS`.\n2. `gerrit_plugin_tests(ext_deps \u003d ...)` is the normal Bazel test deps API and should keep meaning Maven coordinates.\n\nI prepared a compromise (change 598801) along those lines: `gerrit_plugin_ext_test_deps()` creates the Eclipse helper explicitly, `gerrit_plugin_tests(ext_deps \u003d ...)` keeps its current Maven-coordinate semantics so plugins like `oauth` and `javamelody` work as-is, and the new `ext_deps_label` lets callers explicitly reuse the helper target for Bazel tests when they want that.\n\nThere is no implicit *generation* or *auto-discovery* of `\u003cplugin\u003e__plugin_test_deps` from `gerrit_plugin_tests()`. In other words, the common Bazel test-deps case stays simple, and the Eclipse classpath helper is opt-in and explicit.\n\nWDYT? If we agree on that approach, I will abandon this idempotency change.",
      "parentUuid": "9e99f1a3_b5c79722",
      "revId": "5021688dae25fd7638924462fac30d893241095e",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    }
